  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <exercise>
        <problem>
        <para><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_2_12_5_CD_4"/></para>
        </problem>
        </exercise>
      
      <note id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00015">Building Character: Growth Mindset</para>
        
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_14_10_03.png" width="200px"/>
          </media>
        
          
            <para id="para-00016">Compared
        to a fixed mindset, a growth mindset encourages you to embrace challenges, sustain effort,
        and try new strategies. Of course, no one embodies only a growth or fixed mindset; we are
        all a mixture of the two, and we can learn to recognize what triggers a fixed versus growth
        mindset. The brain is like a muscle—something you can strengthen.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Think about
        your current sense of having a growth mindset. Are the following statements are true for
        you?</para>
            <list id="list-00001">
          <item>I truly believe that people can change. </item>
          <item>I can always change how intelligent I am. </item>
        </list>
            <para id="para-00018">Don’t worry
        if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first
        step starts today!</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
